# linux-ccram Kconfig delta over linux-saphira-meta-cram.
#
# CCRAM — AKADATA LIMITED adaptation of Meta CRAM (see CRAM.PROVENANCE
# in linux-saphira-meta-cram; Saphira-original delta, GPL-2.0-only).
#
# Derivation (proven 2026-10-11, reproducible by hand):
#   config-7.2.9-ccram-akadata
#     == config-7.2.9-meta-cram-akadata
#        + the lines below + `make olddefconfig` (ripple checked: only
#          the symbols these select — DRM_CLIENT_SETUP and
#          FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE_DETECT_PRIMARY — may appear; anything
#          else fails the recipe's delta gate).
# Proof command (from the recipe tree root):
#   diff linux-saphira-meta-cram/files/config-7.2.9-meta-cram-akadata \
#        linux-ccram/files/config-7.2.9-ccram-akadata
# yields exactly the LOCALVERSION rename, the CCRAM_SYSRAM line and the
# DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION line.
# Parent config sha256:
#   5d750d6aa2f70424df799c07cf1f9a1f24b50bd8df56ada7c13ed5baa89dcdae
# This config sha256:
#   5967b5926533484590c58fec47460f2db7f3be98e964445c4da8ea8f583e1f35
# The meta-cram config itself derives from config-7.2.2-akadata plus
# cram-config.fragment (see CONFIG-DIFF-JUSTIFICATION.md there), so the
# full chain back to the normal Saphira kernel config is documented.
#
# Release identity: distinct /lib/modules/7.2.9-ccram so every normal
# Saphira kernel keeps its module tree untouched (GRUB fallback stays).
CONFIG_LOCALVERSION="-ccram"
#
# The CCRAM sysram backend itself (bool, default n; Saphira-original).
CONFIG_CCRAM_SYSRAM=y
#
# Legacy fbdev emulation for the modesetting driver (bool, default
# follows FB).  Required on 7.2.9+ for ANY drm framebuffer console:
# the 7.2.9 DRM client rework gates drm_client_setup_* (and hence
# i915's fbdev setup and fbcon takeover) behind this symbol.  Without
# it the driver initialises fully but creates no fb0, fbcon stays on
# the dummy device, and there is no local boot console — unlike the
# 7.2.x Saphira kernels, where the fbdev client was unconditional.
# Selects DRM_CLIENT_SETUP (+ FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE_DETECT_PRIMARY);
# no other ripple (proven by the 2-line diff method in the
# justification document).
CONFIG_DRM_FBDEV_EMULATION=y
#
# Resolution-selected (added by `make olddefconfig`, not part of this
# fragment, asserted present by the recipe's post-resolution gate):
#   CONFIG_DRM_CLIENT_SETUP=y
#   CONFIG_DRM_CLIENT_DEFAULT_FBDEV=y
#   CONFIG_DRM_CLIENT_DEFAULT="fbdev"
#   CONFIG_FRAMEBUFFER_CONSOLE_DETECT_PRIMARY=y
# These four are the documented, intended consequence of the
# FBDEV_EMULATION line above (see drivers/gpu/drm/clients/Kconfig).
# Any other resolution addition fails the build for review.
